$ TMPDIR=/tmp bash tests/fm-secondmate-restart.test.sh
ok - T1 persist is a gate, and asks for open records and task status only
ok - T2 the mate persists before anything is stopped
ok - T2b an arrived persist answer is resolved before timeout
ok - T2c a reply between the preliminary scan and timeout decision wins
ok - T3 a runtime that cannot prove a restart falls back to the re-read message
ok - T4 every named mate is accounted for, including one this home does not know
ok - T5 a refused restart leaves the mate running and reports an unknown outcome
ok - T8 a local restart re-resolves this home's pin and reports the runtime that came up
ok - native Ultra survives local restart and the remote restart transport
ok - T6 a remote mate restarts through the host-local control plane over the fm-on hop
ok - T6a a remote mate with a per-mate override restarts onto that override, not the default pin
ok - T6b a remote mate with no override line still restarts onto the default pin
ok - T6d a legacy pin file still restarts the mate onto its first line
ok - T6c an unreadable per-mate pin falls back to the re-read path with its agent left running
ok - T6b a mate with no recorded code root passes none, so its host keeps its own
ok - T7 an unreachable host is reported honestly instead of claimed as reloaded
ok - T9 the persist gate retains its explicitly allocated correlation
ok - T10 pending persist answers are polled as one fleet
ok - T11 post-stop restart failure is never misreported as a nudge
ok - T12 relaunch waits do not block fleet persistence polling
ok - T13 a dead restart worker cannot hang the parent
ok - T14 a result published during reaping is honored
ok - T15 an already-current live mate is named by the update pass and genuinely restarted
ok - T16 an already-current mate with an unprovable runtime keeps the honest nudge path
ok - T17 a T3 mate is routed to the re-read message by both passes, never restarted
